  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This shawl starts with three chains at the spine and grows by increases at each side edge and the centre spine on every right-side row. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble-fan-l1"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble fan"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " repeat alternates with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "chain-space-l1"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "chain spaces"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to create an open lace fabric. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "top-down-triangle-l1"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "top-down triangle"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " shape means you can stop at any depth you like and the shawl will be complete."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Fingering weight yarn",
              "qty": "400 m"
            },
            {
              "name": "3.5 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Blocking pins and mat",
              "qty": "1 set"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "3 fan repeats x 8 rows = 10 x 10 cm after blocking. Gauge is approximate in lace; finished size is more important than row count."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern notes"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fan repeat (worked over 9 sts): dc, ch 3, skip 3, 5 tr in next st, ch 3, skip 3, dc. On the following row work chain spaces into the tr cluster. The spine increase is 3 tr into the centre chain space on every right-side row."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 6. Row 1 (right side): dc in 4th ch from hook, ch 3, dc in last ch. Turn. (3 sts, 1 ch-sp)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 2 (wrong side): ch 4 (counts as tr), 2 tr in first st, ch 3, 3 tr in last st. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 3 (right side): ch 3 (counts as dc), "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble-fan-l1"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "fan"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " in ch-sp, ch 3, 5 tr in centre sp (spine increase), ch 3, fan in ch-sp, dc in top of t-ch. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Continue in pattern, working a fan into each chain space and a 5-tr spine increase at the centre on every right-side row. On wrong-side rows, chain 3 between each cluster. Work to approximately 52 cm depth (about 34 right-side rows) or until yarn is almost used, leaving 2 m for the border."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Border"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Final row: ch 1, dc evenly along each edge. Work 3 dc into each corner point. Join with slip stitch. Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in all ends. Wet the shawl, press out excess water, then pin it to shape on a mat using blocking pins. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking-l1"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " opens the fans and sets the wingspan. Leave flat until fully dry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to crochet next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The crescent lace shawl uses the same fingering yarn with shell stitch rows for a curved shape that sits neatly at the back of the shoulders."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}